  "description": "TranscriptFinalize.Reduce from TranscriptFinalizeState.Initial over input.events in order, on a virtual clock that starts at 0 ms. Document swiftAnchor is the provider's final-transcript wait; the manager's fallback and error handling (BuddyDictationManager.swift:476-606) are anchored on the cases they justify. Event types: turn {transcript, endsTurn} (transcript is the full transcript AssemblyAiTurnTranscriptAssembler composed after the Turn; endsTurn is end_of_turn or turn_is_formatted), keyReleased {hasActiveTranscriptionSession}, termination, error {message}, and advance {ms}, which moves the clock and reduces a deadlineElapsed for every scheduleDeadline timer that comes due, at its due time. input.stalledProvider true means the provider never calls back, so its providerGrace timer is never armed (parity spec STT-05 b). expected.effects has one entry per event: the effects it emitted, in order. Effects are written as 'scheduleDeadline <providerGrace|sessionFallback|defaultFallback> <delay>ms', 'sendForceEndpoint', 'sendTerminate', 'submitTranscript <text>', 'discardEmptyTranscript' and 'cancelDictation <message>'. expected.finishedAtMs is the clock time of the one submitTranscript, discardEmptyTranscript or cancelDictation. Timings are exact; the +/-100 ms wall-clock tolerance applies only to Replay. Parity spec STT-04, STT-05, STT-06, STT-08.",
